# Virtual Environment Setup Instructions

This folder contains the Python virtual environment for this project.
The actual venv files are NOT committed to git (too large and machine-specific).

## Setup Instructions

### Windows (PowerShell)
```powershell
# Navigate to project root
cd C:\path\to\L23

# Create virtual environment using UV
uv venv

# Activate virtual environment
.venv\Scripts\activate

# Install dependencies
uv pip install -r requirements.txt

# Verify installation
python -c "import sklearn, cvxopt, numpy, pandas; print('All dependencies OK')"
```

### Linux/macOS (or WSL)
```bash
# Navigate to project root
cd /path/to/L23

# Create virtual environment using UV
uv venv

# Activate virtual environment
source .venv/bin/activate

# Install dependencies
uv pip install -r requirements.txt

# Verify installation
python -c "import sklearn, cvxopt, numpy, pandas; print('All dependencies OK')"
```

## Why UV?
- 10-100x faster than pip (parallel downloads)
- Better dependency resolution
- Recommended by PROJECT_GUIDELINES.md

## Running the Project
After activating the virtual environment:
```bash
python main.py
```

Or with custom parameters:
```bash
python main.py --C 1.0 --kernel linear --test-size 0.2 --run 1
```
